#
# Here         There              store_id      release_id    layout
# dense/r/     dense_ranges/      s             r             dense
# ragged/comp/ ragged_completed/  residual-rag  comp          ragged
# hyb/v1/      hybrid_observed/   hyb           v1            hybrid
# hyb/v1c/     hybrid_completed/  hyb           v1-completed  hybrid
#
# Each is byte for byte the bundle's, less variants.tsv.gz, variants.tsv.gz.tbi and overview.html:
# a 0.3.0 release is read from its sidecars, never its Variant Table, and with those files gone each
# still gives every answer of the bundle's expected/<release>.json (its contract_reader.py, run with
# ogquery 0.1.0). They are laid out as GWAS Store directories, each holding its Store Release one
# level down; hyb holds two, the case og_local() refuses for a GWAS Store directory. The names are
# short because R CMD check notes a path in the package tarball longer than 100 bytes, and a hybrid
# release's deepest file is 69 bytes below its root: opengwasr/inst/stores/hyb/v1c/ leaves 70.
